;; tests/conformance/ORACLE.edn
;;
;; Machine-readable pin for the conformance oracle: the exact real-Clojure
;; build every golden in this project is generated against. This is the
;; SAME pin as tests/conformance/CLOJURE_VERSION -- that bare one-line file
;; remains the version string every existing tool (tools/gen-golden.bb,
;; tools/gen-pending.sh, tools/jvm-runner.clj, ...) reads, and its format
;; must not change. This file exists alongside it because those callers
;; only need a version *string*, while tools/bootstrap-oracle.sh (and any
;; future tool that needs the git commit, repo URL, or JDK) needs the full
;; pin in one machine-readable place instead of scraped out of prose in
;; COMPATIBILITY.md or a comment in tests/clojure-suite/MANIFEST.sha256.
;;
;; tools/bootstrap-oracle.sh asserts :clojure-version here equals the
;; contents of CLOJURE_VERSION on every run, and hard-fails if they ever
;; disagree -- so the two files cannot silently drift apart. When the pin
;; is bumped, update BOTH files in the same commit (see ORACLE.md's
;; "bumping the pin" section for the full list and order).
{:clojure-version "1.13.0-alpha6"
 :git-tag "clojure-1.13.0-alpha6"
 :commit "15c821d7e7df241c8f9fed42fbc51b09c65b67d9"
 :repo "https://github.com/clojure/clojure"
 :jdk-tested "21"
 :note "The reference implementation for every golden under tests/conformance/ and tests/clojure-suite/. Materialize it locally with tools/bootstrap-oracle.sh; see tests/conformance/ORACLE.md for the full explanation and tests/clojure-suite/MANIFEST.sha256 for the vendored-test-suite provenance that shares this same commit."}
